Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.830 align:start position:0%
 
the numbers are staggering  border patrol sources estimating  criminal organizations took in at least  14 million dollars a day last month from  trafficking over the u.s mexican border  including  women children and families being  trafficked fox nation host larry logan  has covered the smuggling crisis at the  border and she joins us now  to react lara i think when we think of  cartels we think of drugs narcotics  narcotics smuggling what's increasingly  clear is that's only a portion of their  business  human smuggling and increasing piece of  the pie when it comes to their revenue  please tell us about us  well you're absolutely right will and  this has been going on for some time  but it's really become just a  multi-billion dollar business for the  cartels  and uh you know people still think of  them as the old drug trafficking  organizations  but they've expanded into so many other  things and they've become the most  powerful criminal organizations on earth  so what really most americans don't  understand is that when they see this  mass flow of people across the border  what they're looking at has been  described to me as the largest form of  modern slavery in the world  because and i've seen this with my own  eyes so many of the people coming across  will have a little card in their pocket  or a number written down which is a  routing number for a bank account for  the cartel if you haven't paid all of  your fees by the time you cross  they will collect and so many people  when you're in a restaurant in new york  and  you know you and your friends are  talking about oh isn't it wonderful how  these immigrants work  you know two jobs and they're so hard  working well guess what  they're working two jobs a lot of the  time because so much of their money is  going back to those cartels  who are still exploiting them and now  some of them are wearing wristbands  which link to databases and computers  so the cartel is able to track you  wherever you are and of course they can  also keep track of your family  you know on the other side of the border  so there's no escape for these people  and that's just a segment of the  population they'll help they're helping  to usher over the border  uh larry i know you've said this so i  want to follow up on it the southern  border is arguably the most valuable  stretch of ground  in the world tell me about that and the  fact that whether or not you are from  mexico or central america you might be  paying one rate but if you're coming  from china or the middle east you're  paying another rate  yeah well the cartels are extremely good  at exploiting  every single avenue to make as much  money as possible so they know that  if you're coming as a single adult male  it's much harder for you they can charge  more money  they know if you're coming from a  country like china the mexicans don't  want chinese  people there so when the u.s tries to  send them back no mexico is not taking  them  so china anyone with a nexus to  terrorism what  customs and border protection call  special interest aliens or sias you'll  hear that term  they can charge much higher numbers for  them and something else interesting that  we just learned was that in different  parts along the border there are now uh  charging different rates for example in  acuna which is just  across from del rio texas the rate is  lower than it is in  mcallen and rio grande valley and other  places so  but really what this indicates is that  the cartel can set whatever price they  want to  and uh you know when you have people  coming from haiti and countries like  that  they know that you're much more  desperate they know that it's much  harder for you and they charge you more  right all right larry i have less than a  minute but i want to ask you about the  press access at the border the body  administration is boxing out reports  boxing out reporters from seeing what's  going on we have quotes from  photographers who've been covering this  for years and through various  administrations saying it's never been  like this what's your reaction  well there's an extraordinary  photojournalist who has been covering  this for  four years for administrations and  he wrote an editorial in the washington  post john mua who said  you know that he'd never encountered  this before he was having to take  photographs from mexico using a long  lens  and uh this is you know what this is  really about is just hiding the  inescapable fact  that the biden administration is doing  what biden did when he was in the obama  administration and what the trump  administration did  which is uh that they have to at some  point hold people for processing  and when you hold women and children  whether it's behind bars or whether you  call it a cage or a chain link fence  or plastic pods as project veritas you  know released  yesterday in photographs that they  showed and congressman henry cuellar a  democrat  released in photographs from the border  it never looks good it plays on your  heartstrings  it's emotional i've been down there so  many times and my heart is broken for  these families  but it doesn't change the fact that  there is an extraordinary level of  hypocrisy  the biden administration doesn't want  this country to see the scale of this  crisis  they don't want to acknowledge it's a  crisis and they also don't want to  acknowledge that they're doing exactly  what donald trump did  using the same facilities the same  agents the same protocols  except with one very distinct difference  will is  that they are actually releasing a  number of people into the country  without even giving them a notice to  appear in immigration court  leaving it entirely up to those people  and that's bypassing the legal  immigration system  and it's made the border effectively  open and you know i have a colleague  from 60 minutes who's been waiting five  years  to hold his children he's here legally  his youngest daughter was six months old  when he left afghanistan  she's turning six in april six years old  he's been waiting  and that man has just been tortured by  this weight he loves his children more  than anything  and i don't hear anybody talking about  families have been separated in that way  by the legal immigration system what  happens to them now  all right lara logan has no agenda  return to the border is on fox nation  you get more analysis like  that which you just heard here on fox  and friends lara always good to talk to  you thank you  thank you will all right

